Include <stdio.h> where a declaration names a stream.

auth-shadow.c reaches hostfile.h, which declares functions taking a FILE *,
without having made FILE visible.  It compiles elsewhere because <shadow.h>
happens to drag <stdio.h> in on those systems; zedBSD's does not, because it
declares nothing that takes a stream.  Naming the dependency is the fix.

--- a/auth-shadow.c
+++ b/auth-shadow.c
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 #if defined(USE_SHADOW) && defined(HAS_SHADOW_EXPIRE)
 #include <shadow.h>
 #include <stdarg.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
 #include <string.h>
 #include <time.h>
 
